<.header>
  Your profile
  <:subtitle>
    These details fill demand letters when a case does not override them. Import from your macOS Contacts Me card or enter them manually.
  </:subtitle>
</.header>

<div class="content-card mt-2 max-w-2xl">
  <div class="content-card-body">
    <.simple_form for={@form} id="claimant-profile-form" phx-change="validate" phx-submit="save">
      <.input field={@form[:name]} type="text" label="Your name" />
      <.input field={@form[:address]} type="textarea" label="Mailing address" rows="4" />
      <.input field={@form[:phone]} type="text" label="Phone number" />
      <.input field={@form[:email]} type="email" label="Email address" />
      <.input field={@form[:dnc_registration_date]} type="date" label="DNC registration date" />
      <.input field={@form[:small_claims_county]} type="text" label="Small claims county" />

      <:actions>
        <.button phx-disable-with="Saving...">Save profile</.button>
        <.button type="button" phx-click="import_from_contacts" class="btn-secondary">
          Import from Contacts
        </.button>
      </:actions>
    </.simple_form>

    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-600">
      You can also set environment variables such as
      <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1">DNC_MY_ADDRESS</code>
      and <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1">DNC_MY_PHONE</code>
      for CLI exports. Saved profile values take precedence over env vars in the web app.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="content-card mt-6 max-w-2xl">
  <div class="content-card-body">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-zinc-900">USPS Chrome helper</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-600">
      USPS tracking pages often never hydrate in headless Chrome, so Refresh status opens
      the same URL in your real browser. This unpacked extension reads the finished page
      and posts it back to this local app. Only a tracking number you just clicked Refresh
      for is accepted.
    </p>
    <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm text-slate-700">
      <li>Open <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1">chrome://extensions</code></li>
      <li>Turn on Developer mode</li>
      <li>Click Load unpacked and choose this folder:</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-3 break-all rounded-lg bg-slate-100 px-3 py-2 font-mono text-sm text-slate-800">
      {@chrome_extension_dir}
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-600">
      After installing or updating files, click Reload on the extension card, then reload
      this app. You should see “Chrome helper connected” on a case. Click Refresh status;
      keep the USPS tab open until the helper saves the status. Safari can wait — the same
      files can later be converted with
      <code class="rounded bg-slate-100 px-1">xcrun safari-web-extension-converter</code>.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
